-- title:
--   The parity form of cubical Sperner’s theorem
-- statement:
--   Let $n,p$ be natural numbers, and label the grid $\{0,\ldots,p\}^n$ by integers from $0$ through $n$. Assume that a vertex with coordinate $k$ equal to zero does not have label $k$, and that a vertex with coordinate $k$ equal to $p$ has label at most $k$. Use the monotone unit-step triangulation of the cube. Then
--
--   $$|\{\text{complete }n\text{-simplices}\}|\text{ is odd}.$$
--
--   A complete simplex has all labels $0,\ldots,n$, so the theorem in particular guarantees its existence.
-- source:
